{"agent":"fx-roborev-guards","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_landing` uses `git merge-base --is-ancestor sha base` to decide whether the landed fix is on the base branch. Git's `--is-ancestor` exits non-zero when the two commits are the same commit: a commit is not considered its own ancestor. Therefore, if the fix has landed as the current tip of `base_ref` (for example, `main` is already at fix commit `C` and the user runs with `--landed C`), `_landing` returns `(None, \"... is not on 'main' ...\")` and rejects a commit that is plainly on the base. This exactly blocks the “fix already merged as the base tip” case the change is meant to close; use a reachability check that includes equality instead.","digest":"42e9329c869dfd40","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:_landing","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:_landing"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"When the user runs `ddflow bug fixed B256be593f0 --landed <commit> --regression-test <test>` with an open fix task, the code verifies the commit and immediately `return _regression_status(status, ev, G)`. This branch never calls the newly added `_end_fix_task_landed`/`_drop_fix_task` helpers, and `_regression_status` receives neither the open `fx` nor `landing` as arguments, so the open fix task is not closed in the task store. The command still prints `bug ... closed`, but the original B256be593f0 condition persists: the fix task remains open and the gates still demand a commit ahead.","digest":"047334bf07148bfa","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py (new `if landing is not None:` branch)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py (new `if landing is not None:` branch)"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":17717,"diff_sha":"ce8270ddd9952ea30853977145cbd8fae2992f6cfded31c34dd6e0ab6a988f8b","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes i